No, really, -10. 22000 zorkmids gives you 55 bribes,
at level 1, which is plenty sufficient, with luck,
since you only need to advance 17 times if your
first gift of protection is 4, and you are
guaranteed in that case to get to naked AC 1 in 6
bribes, leaving 49 for the other 11 steps, or almost
5 tries each.

That's not something I regularly achieve, it is more
often the case that I run out of money around naked
AC -4 or -5, but it's happened that I got to -10
often enough to be worth describing as a reasonable
goal. Other protection racketeers suggest stopping
at naked AC 1 or 0, but that just leaves me with
money burning a hole in my sack, and I don't need
the burden, so I keep spending the money on
protection until I don't have enough left for a
whole bribe.

Note that you get not just the gold and shops on
DLVL 1-4, but from each mines level at or above
Mines Town, from the first room on DLVL 5, the one
you duck into just to be able to find your way back
if you fall down a trapdoor, and also from grabbing
the first pickaxe you find in mines and going back
to tunnel through levels with vaults, and from doing
regularly spaced tunnels through levels with stray
gold in the rocks. That gets you all the gold except
the stuff for which you need to dig a pit.  For
that, you need either early potions of object
detection or more patience than I can usually
achieve. You also get to clean out the shops in
mines, giving potentially 8 total shops at up to
4000z apiece from which to strip out cash by credit
cloning, four vaults, much stray gold.  I never get
extra gold from selling stuff, since the credit
cloning scam already cleans out every shopkeeper to
the last zorkmid, so stuff like IDing gems to sell
them is a waste of effort.

I usually do the protection in two steps, to improve
survival, buying what I can immediately as I arrive
at Mines Town and find the priest, _then_ doing
credit cloning in the local shops. This can find me
doing the Mines Town credit cloning at AC -5 or
better, from armor gathered in the upper levels of
mines, at which point with still XL 1, the monsters
are so wimpy I can usually just let them bash on me
until I find a pet or a pet finds me, and I try to
have my pet in or near the shop, obviously, since a
pet is an essential part of credit cloning.

All this put together, it isn't unusual at all for
my to achieve XL2 only after 12,000 or so turns.

There are also _lots_ of circumstances in which the
protection racket gets abandoned; pets killed early,
altar found in upper main dungeon, pets ignoring me
so that I get pushed past XL 1 too early, pets dying
picking fights with the Mines Town watch so that I
can't credit clone the Mines Town shops. The
protection racket is an ideal, it doesn't always
work, but when it works, my survival is much better
further on in the game than with the alternative,
combat wombat behaviors that have me fighting
nastier monsters my AC is not fit to face, and any
part of the protection racket being successful up my
PC's longevity.

